# Ignore file for frontend/Dockerfile only. BuildKit (the default builder in
# current Docker and Compose) reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in place of the
# context-root .dockerignore; the legacy builder falls back to the root file.
#
# The build context is the repository root, and the root file's
# `node_modules/` matches ./node_modules only -- dockerignore patterns are
# anchored at the context root. So the host's frontend/node_modules (93 MB
# here) was sent to the builder, and `COPY frontend/ .` laid it over the tree
# `npm ci` had just installed, mixing host-platform packages (a Windows
# host's, say) into a Linux image built from the lockfile.
#
# Allowlist: this image needs frontend/ and sdk/ and nothing else. That also
# keeps data/ (recorded real sessions) and .env out of the context.
*
!frontend
!sdk

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
